	{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"Person","name":"Romal  Shetty","image":"https://www.deloitte.com/content/dam/assets-zone1/in/en/img/profiles/q-t/in-profile-romal-shetty-noexp.png","jobTitle":"Chief Executive Officer | Deloitte South Asia","description":"Romal Shetty is the Chief Executive Officer of Deloitte South Asia.&nbsp;He is also a member of Deloitte’s Global Executive Committee.

In his more than two decades of work experience, Romal has led large transformation programmes across more than 40 countries for Indian and global clients, to shape their growth strategies, profitability, restructuring, technology, and people agenda. In the past five years, he has led the growth of the consulting practice from 2,000 to over 10,000 people, with India being the fastest-growing practice across the Deloitte network.

Romal is a fierce believer in Purpose and rallying people to a common cause. He has successfully led signature community initiatives at Deloitte in collaboration with various state governments. These include initiatives like Anemia Mukt Bharat, Sanjeevani Pariyojana, anti-erosion embankment project, and Stubble burning.

A people’s leader, Romal’s core values include stewardship of exceptional talent, client centricity, integrity, and learning from failures. He is a trusted Advisor and possesses strong relationships with Board of Directors, CEOs, CFOs, CHROs, CTOs, and Strategy Directors across sectors.

He is a Fellow Member of the ICAI and a Certified Information Systems Auditor. He has also completed the Executive Leadership International program at INSEAD.

A proud Indian, Romal lives in Bangalore with his wife, Akila and their son, Ayaan. Romal is passionate about sports, especially Cricket, and often finds analogies and lessons that can be applied in business.
